 "_interpretation": "Without TTA (as M4), log 10: knot IoU 2d 0.768, 3d_z7 0.763, 3d_z5 0.767 vs M4 0.763; bootstraps vs M4 +0.005 [-0.004, +0.015], +0.000 [-0.014, +0.015], +0.004 [-0.008, +0.018]: one nnU-Net = the two-model M4 on pixels. Instances are better for all three: mAP50 0.898-0.915 vs 0.877, mAP50-95 0.532-0.538 vs 0.513, thin AP50 0.70-0.74 vs 0.65. 3D context mainly helps thin-knot recall (3d_z7 0.846, 3d_z5 0.795, 2d 0.744, M4 0.718 = 33/31/29/28 of 39 thin knots), not pixels: 3d_z7 - 2d -0.005 [-0.011, +0.002], 3d_z5 - 3d_z7 +0.004 [-0.000, +0.008] (5 slices slightly better than 7). Isolated-thin rate (thin predictions without overlap in k+-1; human GT 7.7%): 2d 4.6%, 3d_z5 6.4%, 3d_z7 8.9%, M4 10.5%; counts are ~40 thin components, so these are noisy. TTA (mirroring) adds +0.000 to +0.004 pixel IoU (2d +0.000, 3d_z7 +0.002, 3d_z5 +0.004), within noise; conclusions are the same with or without it. Fit on the human training logs 1/2/4: 0.85-0.88 for every nnU-Net configuration vs 0.76-0.79 for M4 (the under-fitting correction stands). Single runs; seed noise ~0.018 on log 10.",
